<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">16 April in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 16 April, from 1457 BCE to 2007.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/thutmose-iii" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thutmose-iii.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1457 BCE <span class="tih-ago">3,482 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Thutmose III defeats a Canaanite coalition at Megiddo</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pharaoh">Pharaoh</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thutmose-iii">Thutmose III</a> routed a coalition led by the king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-kadesh">Kadesh</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-megiddo">Megiddo</a>, on a date traditionally reckoned to 16 April. His annals give the first detailed account of a battle in recorded history.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thutmose-iii">Thutmose III</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">73 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,953 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Romans breach the walls of Masada</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After a siege of probably two to three months, Roman forces breached the wall of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/masada">Masada</a>, the last rebel stronghold of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-jewish-roman-war">First Jewish–Roman War</a>, with a battering ram. According to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/josephus">Josephus</a>, its defenders killed themselves rather than surrender.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/masada">Masada</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-jewish-roman-war">First Jewish–Roman War</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">556 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,470 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Pelagius I becomes pope as the candidate of Justinian I</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Pelagius I became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> as the candidate of Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/justinian-i">Justinian I</a>, a choice not well received in the Western Church. Before his <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/papacy">papacy</a> he had opposed Justinian's efforts to condemn the Three Chapters, but later adopted the emperor's position.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/justinian-i">Justinian I</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1346">1346 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">680 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Stefan Dušan is crowned Emperor of the Serbs at Skopje</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stefan-dusan">Stefan Dušan</a>, King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbia">Serbia</a> since 1331, was crowned Emperor of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbs">Serbs</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greeks">Greeks</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/skopje">Skopje</a>, founding the Serbian Empire. It became the largest Balkan state of its day but broke apart soon after his death in 1355.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stefan-dusan">Stefan Dušan</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/skopje">Skopje</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1746">1746 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">280 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Jacobite army is crushed at Culloden</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Government troops under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ernest-augustus-king-of-hanover">Duke of Cumberland</a> routed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-edward-stuart">Charles Edward Stuart</a>'s army near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inverness">Inverness</a> in under an hour. It was the last pitched battle on British soil and was followed by harsh repression in the Highlands.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1856">1856 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">170 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Powers sign the Paris Declaration on maritime law</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Meeting at the Congress of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a>, the great powers agreed to abolish privateering and protect neutral goods at sea. It was the first multilateral treaty codifying the laws of naval warfare.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1917">1917 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">109 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Lenin arrives at Petrograd's Finland Station</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Returning from Swiss exile with German help, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vladimir-lenin">Vladimir Lenin</a> was greeted by crowds in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/petrograd">Petrograd</a>. His call to oppose the Provisional Government set the Bolsheviks on the road to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/october-revolution">October Revolution</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/petrograd">Petrograd</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/finland">Finland</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1943">1943 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">83 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Albert Hofmann experiences the effects of LSD by accident</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Working at Sandoz in Basel, chemist Albert Hofmann absorbed a trace of LSD and felt its effects. Three days later, on 19 April, he took a deliberate dose to test it.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/2007">2007 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">19 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Gunman kills 32 people at Virginia Tech</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A student shot dead 32 people on the campus in Blacksburg, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virginia">Virginia</a>, before killing himself. It was then the deadliest shooting by a lone gunman in US history and led to reforms of background checks.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virginia">Virginia</a></div></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 16 April <span class="n">2</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/tabinshwehti"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/tabinshwehti.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Tabinshwehti</span><span class="tp">1516–1550</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/margrethe-ii"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/margrethe-ii.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Margrethe II</span><span class="tp">b. 1940</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 16 April <span class="n">6</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/sichelgaita"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Sichelgaita</span><span class="tp">c. 1040–1090</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/sviatopolk-ii-of-kiev"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/sviatopolk-ii-of-kiev.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Sviatopolk II of Kiev</span><span class="tp">1050–1113</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/adelaide-del-vasto"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/adelaide-del-vasto.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Adelaide del Vasto</span><span class="tp">c. 1075–1118</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/aphra-behn"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/aphra-behn.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Aphra Behn</span><span class="tp">1640–1689</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/emilio-jacinto"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/emilio-jacinto.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Emilio Jacinto</span><span class="tp">1875–1899</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/jose-carlos-mariategui"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/jose-carlos-mariategui.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">José Carlos Mariátegui</span><span class="tp">1894–1930</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
